# Notion project manager

After we build, fix, change, decide, or finish something, update Notion before the reply ends. Skip this when Mark only asked a question.

## Find the project

- Business: "🗂 Projects" — collection://3ff8f107-01a5-4292-b4f7-e4731437932a
- Personal: "🌱 Personal Projects" — collection://60b0c57d-dfda-4de9-b0f3-22a5c7b14ca6
- Search by project name. No match: create a row with Project, Status, Area, Owner, Summary, Where it lives.

## Update that row only

- Status: ✅ Live, 🔨 Building, 🧪 Testing, ⏳ Waiting on Mark, ⛔ Blocked, 💡 Idea, or 🗄 Done
- Next step: one line
- Waiting on Mark: what he personally has to do, or blank
- Last update: today's date
- Page body, under `## History` (create it if missing), add one line at the bottom: `- YYYY-MM-DD — what changed` in plain English
- Personal projects: also refresh Open items

## Log tasks

"✅ Tasks" — collection://f79e78c4-a789-4ba0-9cf2-15ebef6957c2

- One row per finished piece of work. Check for a matching task first. Do not duplicate.
- Task = short name. Project = the row above. Status = Done. Owner = Mark, Kat, Jayden, or Claude.
- Work left for Mark: a separate task, Status "Waiting on Mark", Waiting on Mark checkbox ticked.

Never delete or overwrite rows in bulk.

End the reply with one line: `📒 Logged to Notion: [project] → History + N tasks Done.`

If Notion is unreachable, say so and give Mark the update text to paste.
